    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d443">

                <pb facs="0420" n="346" xml:id="pg346"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Bigelow</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 271.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <hi
                                rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-09-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >September</hi> 25, 1865.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have received your despatch of the 2d
                    instant, No. 168, enclosing copies of the replies which you made, in compliance
                    with my instructions, to the letters of condolence and sympathy which were
                    inspired by the death of the late President, and addressed to this government by
                    various political and social organizations in France. In reply, I beg that you
                    will accept my thanks for the prompt and efficient manner in which you performed
                    the duty assigned to you, and I desire, at the same time, to inform you of my
                    high appreciation of the communications which you have been pleased to submit to
                    me as the result of your labor.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Bigelow,</hi> Esq., <hi rendition="#italic"
                            >&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
